ATTEMPT: 1
---
Setup: worked in a `cp -a` copy at /tmp/claude-1000/.../z5check/budget2 (real repo untouched).
Confirmed foreign uncommitted edits (Z1-Z4 territory) present as declared:
handlers_sweep*.go, sync*.go, present_value.go — not touched by Z5's diff,
attributed accordingly and not used against this verdict.

git diff --stat for Z5's 6 claimed files matches the manifest (188+/1-,
6 files). `go build ./...` and `go vet ./...` both clean.
`go test ./internal/services/retirement/... ./internal/handlers/whatif/...
-count=1` — all packages pass, including the two new Z5 tests.

Attack angles tried:

1. Stale-name-after-transition-to-disabled (recording site, engine level).
   Wrote TestZ5Probe_TransitionToDisabledClearsPhaseName: chain from a
   phases-ENABLED base scenario to a phases-DISABLED linked scenario at a
   year boundary. Result: year0="Go-Go", year1="", year2="" — the engine
   correctly CLEARS CurrentPhaseName post-transition (GetSpendingPhaseNameAt
   returns "" when disabled, and it's recomputed unconditionally every
   month with m>0). REFUTED at the engine layer — no stale name there.

2. Immediate (year-0 / month-0) transition, where TransitionAge <= primary
   CurrentAge fires ResolveChain at m=0 itself, outside the `if m > 0`
   guard that updates CurrentPhaseName. Wrote
   TestZ5Probe_ImmediateTransitionAtYearZero: year0 correctly shows
   "Immediate-Phase" (the post-transition scenario), because months 1-11
   of that same year (all m>0) overwrite the month-0 stale value before
   finalizeCurrentYear reads it at year-end. REFUTED for any realistic
   (>=1 full year) run. Noted but not failed on: a depletion at month 0
   itself combined with an immediate chain transition would read the
   pre-transition month-0 seed value — this mirrors a PRE-EXISTING `if m >
   0` convention already used for CurrentLivingExpenses/CumulativeInflation
   in this same function, not a Z5-introduced gap, and is a maximally
   degenerate corner case (zero-progress depletion) outside realistic
   acceptance scope.

3. Mid-year transitions: the chain-resolution call site only runs at
   `monthInYear == 0` (once per year); TransitionAge comparisons are in
   whole years (`primarySettings.CurrentAge + currentYear`). Transitions in
   this engine structurally CANNOT occur mid-year — confirmed by reading
   engine_hooks.go's nextChainTransitionForEngine. Attack angle inapplicable
   to this design.

4. Twin derivation-site check (stepper.go ~247 living-expenses multiplier
   vs ~292-296 expense-sources multiplier) vs the new CurrentPhaseName
   write (~246): both multiplier call sites and the phase-name write share
   the same local `s` and the same `phaseAge` computed once at the top of
   StepMonth. Consistent by construction; no divergence found.

5. FOUND A REAL DEFECT — handler-level fallback conflates two different
   meanings of an empty PhaseName. buildSpendingTrajectoryRows falls back
   to trajectoryPhaseName(s, yi) — computed from the PRIMARY settings
   passed into the handler — whenever the summary's PhaseName is "". But
   "" is now overloaded: it means EITHER (a) no data (pre-field
   projection, or no chain — the case the worker tested), OR (b) the
   engine legitimately recorded no active phase for that year because the
   CHAIN-ACTIVE settings for that year had phases disabled (proven
   reachable by probe #1 above). In case (b), the fallback ignores the
   engine's correct "no phase" determination and instead shows a label
   computed from the PRIMARY (pre-transition) scenario's phase config —
   the exact "phase labels must follow scenario-chain transitions"
   requirement the task exists to satisfy, violated for this case.

   Reproduced directly against the production function with
   TestZ5Probe_FallbackMasksLegitimateEmptyPhaseName (primary settings:
   phases enabled Go-Go@0/Slow-Go@66; YearlySummaries: year0
   PhaseName="Go-Go", year1 PhaseName="" — the exact shape probe #1 proved
   the engine emits for a chain-transition-to-disabled year):
     go test ./internal/handlers/whatif/... -run TestZ5Probe_FallbackMasksLegitimateEmptyPhaseName -v
   Result: row[1].PhaseName == "Slow-Go" (the PRIMARY's post-Slow-Go-age
   label) instead of "-"/empty (no phase active that year per the engine).
   FAIL — a plan with a scenario chain into a phases-disabled linked
   scenario shows a stale, contradicted phase label on the spending
   trajectory table for every post-transition year.

   This is squarely in scope: same function (buildSpendingTrajectoryRows)
   and same design point (the "" sentinel and its fallback) the worker
   wrote for this task; the worker's own two new handler tests exercise
   only the "chain gives a real name" case and the "everything disabled/no
   chain, both primary and summary agree" case — never the divergent
   combination (primary enabled, summary legitimately empty from a
   disabled post-transition scenario) that actually breaks. The manifest's
   own note ("falling back to trajectoryPhaseName(s, yi) when the summary
   has no name (no chain, or a projection built before this field
   existed)") states an incomplete list of when "" occurs — it omits the
   chain-to-disabled case, which is the bug.

6. Serialization/consumers: grepped all non-test consumers of
   YearlySummaries/ProjectionYearSummary (analysis/tax.go,
   analysis/present_value.go, analysis/tax_optimizer*.go,
   analysis/explainability.go, mcpsvc/plan/view.go, handlers_sweep.go) —
   no positional (unkeyed) struct literals of ProjectionYearSummary (build
   would have failed), no golden-file/testdata fixtures asserting on
   YearlySummaries JSON shape found repo-wide. No breakage found on this
   angle.

Probe files (z5_probe_test.go, z5_probe2_test.go) written only in the
throwaway /tmp copy; not committed to the real tree.

Verdict: FAIL. Item 5 is a real, in-scope, reachable defect — the handler's
empty-string fallback re-derives a phase label from the primary/pre-transition
settings for years where the engine correctly recorded "no active phase"
because the chain transitioned to phases-disabled settings, directly
contradicting the task's own purpose (labels must follow scenario-chain
transitions).
